00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:27,180
Whenever we talk about electrical, then ELCB and RCCB are the most confusing terms.

204
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:32,180
So you should know what is the difference between ELCB and RCCB.

205
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:34,180
So let's see.

206
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:38,180
The full form of ELCB is Earth-Liquid Circuit Breaker.

207
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:42,180
And the full form of RCCB is Residual Current Circuit Breaker.

208
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:46,180
RCCB is the updated version of ELCB.

209
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:51,180
And these days it has been completely replaced by RCCB.

210
00:10:51,180 --> 00:10:55,180
So let's know what ELCB means first.

211
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:58,180
ELCB means Earth-Liquid Circuit Breaker.

212
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:01,180
Now let's see how it works.

213
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:05,180
The green wire that we connect in ELCB is called Earth.

214
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:10,180
And its earth terminal is connected through a sensitive block.

215
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:14,180
So what happens in ELCB is that incoming power comes.

216
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:16,180
A red and a black.

217
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:19,180
That means you can call it face or neutral.

218
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:23,180
And its outgoing power is red and black.

219
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:25,180
That means phase or neutral.

220
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:29,180
That means phase or neutral is incoming power and its outgoing power is also there.

221
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:35,180
That incoming power and outgoing power are connected through a sensitive tripping block.

222
00:11:35,180 --> 00:11:39,180
And that sensitive tripping block is connected through the earthing wire.

223
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:46,180
If the outgoing red color wire is accidentally contacted by the green color wire.

224
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:50,180
Then the red wire of the face and the green ground wire.

225
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:53,180
The current flowing in it will get leakage.

226
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:58,180
Because of which the tripping coil starts to get voltage drop.

227
00:11:58,180 --> 00:12:03,180
This voltage drop is enough to activate the trip circuit.

228
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:08,180
That means that voltage drop will activate the trip circuit.

229
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:11,180
And finally the ELCB will be open.

230
00:12:11,180 --> 00:12:14,180
That means it will be isolated from its source.

231
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:18,180
That means it will isolate the source from that file.

232
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:22,180
Now let's understand how the function of RCCB is.

233
00:12:22,180 --> 00:12:26,180
RCCB means residual current circuit breaker.

234
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:31,180
RCCB works under the principle of core balance current transformer.

235
00:12:31,180 --> 00:12:35,180
So the main function of RCCB is monitoring.

236
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:39,180
What it does is that the phase wire and the neutral wire.

237
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:43,180
It monitors how much current is flowing in it.

238
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:50,180
Especially the load is connected across the phase and neutral terminals.

239
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:54,180
That means in RCCB the core balance current transformer.

240
00:12:54,180 --> 00:12:59,180
It monitors how much current is flowing in the phase and neutral.

241
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:03,180
That means how much current is flowing in the phase wire.

242
00:13:03,180 --> 00:13:07,180
And how much current is coming back from the neutral wire.

243
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:12,180
That means if the current is flowing in the phase wire.

244
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:19,180
Then obviously the same current is coming back from the neutral wire.

245
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:23,180
That means the current flow of these two will be the same.

246
00:13:23,180 --> 00:13:27,180
It will be zero in its core balance current transformer.

247
00:13:27,180 --> 00:13:31,180
At that time RCCB will not operate in that normal condition.

248
00:13:31,180 --> 00:13:34,180
Let's consider that if someone falls.

249
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:38,180
Or if a person touches the live phase wire.

250
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:42,180
Because of which the live wire and earth.

251
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:45,180
The current flow between these two will get leakage.

252
00:13:45,180 --> 00:13:50,180
That means the existing load of the phase was 20 mA.

253
00:13:50,180 --> 00:13:53,180
Now when a person touches the phase.

254
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:55,180
The current flow from that is leakage.

255
00:13:55,180 --> 00:14:00,180
That means the fault current and leakage current will get increased.

256
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:02,180
That means now it will be 30 mA.

257
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:06,180
But our neutral wire was carrying 20 mA.

